# Legacy MCP permission wrapper: its dist/mcp/permissionServer.js target is
# not built. The Claude bridge now uses --permission-prompt-tool stdio and
# resources/claude-policy/settings.json; this obsolete entrypoint stays out.
resources/mcp-permission-server.js

# Playwright is a webpack EXTERNAL (webpack.config.js), so it is required from
# node_modules at RUNTIME rather than bundled — playwright-core locates browser
# drivers by filesystem path and does not survive bundling. Without these
# un-ignores every packaged build fails `require('playwright')` and visual
# testing is dead on arrival in the VSIX. The browser BINARIES are not shipped
# (hundreds of MB); the user installs them via `npx playwright install chromium`.
#
# These two un-ignores only do anything when vsce is collecting dependencies:
# `vsce package --no-dependencies` never walks node_modules at all, so there is
# nothing for a `!` rule to re-include and the packaged extension silently ships
# without Playwright. Measured on this tree: `vsce ls` = 677 files, `vsce ls
# --no-dependencies` = 135, and the entire 542-file difference is Playwright.
# That is why `npm run package` pins `vsce package --dependencies`.
# The `!(*.d.ts)` is load-bearing and must not be "simplified" to `**`.
#
# vsce does NOT resolve these patterns last-match-wins by position: it collects
# every `!` rule and re-includes anything matching ANY of them, after all the
# ignore rules have run. So a plain `!node_modules/playwright/**` overrides
# `**/*.ts` at the top of this file unconditionally and drags in Playwright's
# TypeScript declarations — 2.03 MB across 9 files, playwright-core/types/
# types.d.ts alone being 922 KB. Nothing reads a .d.ts at runtime.
#
# Appending `node_modules/playwright/**/*.d.ts` BELOW these lines does not work;
# it was measured (`vsce ls` stayed at 686 files, all 9 declarations still
# listed). The exclusion has to be expressed inside the negation itself, which
# is what the extglob does.
#
# Measured with `npx @vscode/vsce@3.9.2 ls`: 686 files with a bare `**`
# negation, 677 with this one, and the difference is exactly those 9 `.d.ts` —
# all 542 Playwright RUNTIME files are still shipped. Verify with `node
# scripts/check-package-shape.js` (assertions C and D) after any change here:
# getting it wrong ships an extension whose `require('playwright')` throws.
!node_modules/playwright/**/!(*.d.ts)
!node_modules/playwright-core/**/!(*.d.ts)

# The four `contributes.walkthroughs` step images live under docs/, which is
# ignored above — so in every packaged install four of the five walkthrough
# steps rendered with a broken image. They are re-included here rather than
# relocated because the same files are referenced by all 11 README translations
# (the Marketplace rewrites relative README paths against the repository).
!docs/screenshots/quick-actions-welcome.png
!docs/screenshots/settings-panel.png
!docs/screenshots/user-experience.png
!docs/screenshots/brainstorm-mode.png
